{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"cbb507d751e132d2","name":"card_event_rising_sun","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/Base/events/card_event_rising_sun","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"EXPANSION","text":"If you control a Japanese unit in the frontline, draw 2 cards.","flavorText":"Following the attack on Pearl Harbor in December 1941 the Japanese had a long series of military successes in Asia and the Pacific. That same month Thailand surrendered to the Japanese only 5 hours into the invasion, and Hong Kong, Guam and Wake Island fell shortly after. In January 1942 Manila, the capital city of the Philippines, was occupied, Singapore was conquered in February and Rangoon (Burma) and the Dutch East Indies fell in early March. It wasn’t until the mid year of 1942 that the forces of Australia and New Zealand in New Guinea and the British forces in India managed to halt the Japanese advance. Furthermore, the Japanese Navy had not managed to drive the US Navy out of the South Pacific and would soon receive a crippling blow in the Battle of Midway, which is considered to be a turning point in the Battle of the Pacific. After that the Allied forces slowly gained air and naval supremacy in the Pacific and the tables were turned. ","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_rising_sun","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_rising_sun_title","SourceString":"EXPANSION","LocalizedString":"EXPANSION"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_rising_sun_text","SourceString":"If you control a Japanese unit in the frontline, draw 2 cards.","LocalizedString":"If you control a Japanese unit in the frontline, draw 2 cards."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_rising_sun_history","SourceString":"Following the attack on Pearl Harbor in December 1941 the Japanese had a long series of military successes in Asia and the Pacific. That same month Thailand surrendered to the Japanese only 5 hours into the invasion, and Hong Kong, Guam and Wake Island fell shortly after. In January 1942 Manila, the capital city of the Philippines, was occupied, Singapore was conquered in February and Rangoon (Burma) and the Dutch East Indies fell in early March. It wasn’t until the mid year of 1942 that the forces of Australia and New Zealand in New Guinea and the British forces in India managed to halt the Japanese advance. Furthermore, the Japanese Navy had not managed to drive the US Navy out of the South Pacific and would soon receive a crippling blow in the Battle of Midway, which is considered to be a turning point in the Battle of the Pacific. After that the Allied forces slowly gained air and naval supremacy in the Pacific and the tables were turned. ","LocalizedString":"Following the attack on Pearl Harbor in December 1941 the Japanese had a long series of military successes in Asia and the Pacific. That same month Thailand surrendered to the Japanese only 5 hours into the invasion, and Hong Kong, Guam and Wake Island fell shortly after. In January 1942 Manila, the capital city of the Philippines, was occupied, Singapore was conquered in February and Rangoon (Burma) and the Dutch East Indies fell in early March. It wasn’t until the mid year of 1942 that the forces of Australia and New Zealand in New Guinea and the British forces in India managed to halt the Japanese advance. Furthermore, the Japanese Navy had not managed to drive the US Navy out of the South Pacific and would soon receive a crippling blow in the Battle of Midway, which is considered to be a turning point in the Battle of the Pacific. After that the Allied forces slowly gained air and naval supremacy in the Pacific and the tables were turned. "},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Basic","isInPermanentPool":true,"soundE